From 411f2721847970a477b1d5a7442fedf7237797a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tung Son Do <dosontung007@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:12:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ollama): opt-in native api that sends num_ctx for
 implicit Ollama

Over the OpenAI-compatible endpoint a local Ollama server loads every model at
its own default context (4096 on most GPUs), which is smaller than the agent's
first request, so the first turn fails with exceed_context_size_error.

PI_OLLAMA_API=ollama-chat switches the implicit Ollama provider to the native
/api/chat, which now sends the model's context window as options.num_ctx. The
window is the discovered context capped at OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH, or 16384 when
it is unset. Native-api discovery rows use the root base URL and a separate
cache namespace. The default stays openai-responses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
